userStories.description:
**Goal** — Compose the local memory host and expose live merged note reads and keyword search.

**Motivation** — The koda provider (feature 3) and run stages (feature 4) build on the host and config added here.

**Approach** — Composition: `memoryDirs` → `createMemoryStore({ projectDir, userDir, logger })` → `createMemoryOutbox({ dir: store.paths.outboxDir })` → `createLocalMemoryProvider(store)`. Repo notes are read on each call of `notes`, `getNote`, `search`, `renderIndex` and `status` (no cache). The host hands `readRepoNotes` a wrapper of its logger that drops a `warn` whose `message`, `path` and `reason` it has already passed on, so one bad repo note warns once per host, not once per call.
- `notes("project")` = the mirror's project notes plus every repo note whose slug the mirror's project notes do not hold (the agent's own note shadows the team note), sorted by slug in code-point order; `notes("user")` = the mirror's user notes, sorted the same way.
- `getNote(scope, slug)` = the matching element of `notes(scope)` or `null`.
- `search` = `searchMemoryNotes(notes, text, limit)` over `notes("project")` + `notes("user")` when `scope` is absent, else over `notes(scope)`.

`_memoryHostDeps = { memoryDirs, readRepoNotes, createMemoryStore, createMemoryOutbox, createLocalMemoryProvider, syncMemory, saveMemoryNote, forgetMemoryNote, approveMemoryNote }`.

**Scope** — In: host.ts complete interface, composition, disabled short-circuit, dirs/providerId/writeMode, reads/search, logger wrapper and barrel exports. Out: index/sync/status implementations (US-006), writes/read-only refusal (US-007); `renderIndex`, `sync`, `status`, `save`, `forget` and `approve` throw `NaxError` `MEMORY_NOT_IMPLEMENTED` until US-006 and US-007. No changes to nax-agent.

**Interface**
```ts
export interface MemoryStatus {
  readonly enabled: true;
  readonly provider: string;                 // "local"
  readonly writeMode: "direct" | "proposal";
  readonly projectDir: string;
  readonly userDir: string;
  readonly lastPullAt: string | null;        // from sync.json
  readonly lastError: string | null;
  readonly queued: number;                   // outbox entries in state "queued"
  readonly rejected: number;                 // outbox entries in state "rejected"
  readonly notes: { readonly project: number; readonly user: number; readonly repo: number };
  readonly repoSkipped: number;              // RepoNotes.skipped
}
export interface MemoryHost {
  readonly dirs: MemoryDirs;
  readonly providerId: string;
  readonly writeMode: "direct" | "proposal";
  notes(scope: MemoryScope): Promise<readonly MemoryNote[]>;
  getNote(scope: MemoryScope, slug: string): Promise<MemoryNote | null>;
  search(input: { readonly text: string; readonly scope?: MemoryScope; readonly limit: number }): Promise<readonly MemoryHit[]>;
  renderIndex(): Promise<RenderedMemoryIndex>;
  sync(): Promise<MemorySyncResult>;
  status(): Promise<MemoryStatus>;
  save(write: MemoryNoteWrite): Promise<MemorySaveResult>;
  forget(input: { readonly scope: MemoryScope; readonly slug: string; readonly reason: string }): Promise<MemoryForgetResult>;
  approve(input: { readonly scope: MemoryScope; readonly slug: string }): Promise<MemoryNote>;
}
export async function createMemoryHost(input: {
  readonly config: NaxConfig;
  readonly repoRoot: string;
  readonly source: string;   // "nax-chat" for chat, "human" for the CLI
  readonly logger: MemoryLogger;
}): Promise<MemoryHost | null>;   // null when memoryConfigOf(config).enabled is false
```
